Hi,

I am currently working on a paper that uses an R command line app. For this, I want to save the legend of a gplot into a file and also save the plot itself to another file.

That is all fine and nice, but I need to know the height and width of the legend before saving it to disk. ggsave or cairo_pdf (which we use) require manual adjustment to the shape of the object to save or they take the defaults of 7x7 which looks rather strange for legend that is, e.g. 2 lines in height.

here is my code to extract the legend:

g_legend<-function(a.gplot){
  tmp <- ggplot_gtable(ggplot_build(a.gplot))
  leg <- which(sapply(tmp$grobs, function(x) x$name) == "guide-box")
  legend <- tmp$grobs[[leg]]
  return(legend)
}

legend <- g_legend(some_plot)
cairo_pdf("some.pdf",width=??,height=??)

I am struggling since a couple of hours to retrieve the height and width of the legend to replace the "??" with.

I'd appreciate any help or pointers to possible solutions,
thanks -
Peter

